  "title": "Order allocation: stock lots, inclusive expiry, partial shipments, a lot limit",
  "proves": ["a lot may serve an order only for the product of the order (A3)", "a lot may ship on its expiry date, and not on the day after (A1)", "no lot ships more than its quantity (A2)", "an order that does not allow a partial shipment is filled completely (A4), and no order uses more lots than the policy allows (A5): O8 needs three lots, ships 6 of 8 from two and back-orders 2 while a third lot stays unused", "an order that allows a partial shipment ships all stock that is still good on its ship date, and the rest is back-ordered (A4)", "the search needs a backtrack: the first lots by expiry leave a later order without stock", "a demand that no allocation can meet is reported as infeasible, and an exhausted budget is reported as not proven", "the decision evidence names for each eligible lot of an order one reason word (used, A2, A5, not_needed) and a detail; the checks count the lots without a reason (unexplained == 0) and pin the A5 lot of O8", "the same model, data and seed give the same allocation on every run"],
